### Madre Pulse API — manual verification requests
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy into curl/Postman.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### Health check (Slice 0)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Register (Slice 1) — creates org + admin user, sets refresh cookie
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orgName": "Acme Inc",
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada@acme.test",
  "password": "correcthorse123"
}

### Login (Slice 1)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@acme.test",
  "password": "correcthorse123"
}

### Me (Slice 1) — requires accessToken from register/login response
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Refresh (Slice 1) — uses the refresh_token cookie set by register/login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh

### Logout (Slice 1) — revokes the refresh cookie's token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

### Get organization settings (Slice 17) — any authenticated role
GET {{baseUrl}}/organization
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Rename the organization (Slice 17) — ADMIN only
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/organization
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme Incorporated"
}

### Platform admin (Slice 18) — superadmin only (User.isSuperAdmin, set directly in the DB, see DEVELOPER.md).
### {{login}} must belong to a superadmin account for these to succeed — a normal ADMIN gets 403.

### List every organization on the platform
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/organizations
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Change an organization's plan
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/organizations/{{register.response.body.org.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "plan": "PRO"
}

### Suspend an organization — blocks its login/refresh going forward
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/organizations/{{register.response.body.org.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "SUSPENDED"
}

### Google Meet integration (Slice 19) — step 1 only: connect/disconnect. No transcript endpoints yet.
### Requires GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/SECRET/REDIRECT_URI/TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY configured — see DEVELOPER.md.

### Check whether this org has connected Google Workspace
GET {{baseUrl}}/integrations/google/status
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Get the OAuth consent URL — ADMIN only. Open the returned `url` in a real browser to complete
### the flow (this can't be exercised as a plain HTTP request — Google needs an actual sign-in).
GET {{baseUrl}}/integrations/google/connect-url
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Disconnect Google Workspace — ADMIN only
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/integrations/google
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Platform AI provider settings (Slice 20) — superadmin only, platform-wide (not per-org).
### {{login}} must belong to a superadmin account — see Slice 18's block above for how to become one.

### Check whether an LLM API key is configured (never returns the key itself)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/llm-settings
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Set or replace the platform's LLM API key
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/llm-settings
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "apiKey": "sk-ant-your-real-key-here",
  "model": "claude-sonnet-5"
}

### List members (Slice 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Add a member (Slice 2) — ADMIN only
# @name addMember
POST {{baseUrl}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mia@acme.test",
  "name": "Mia Manager",
  "role": "MANAGER"
}

### Update a member's role/status (Slice 2) — ADMIN only
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/members/{{addMember.response.body.member.membershipId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "DISABLED"
}

### List clients (Slice 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/clients
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Add a client (Slice 2) — ADMIN or MANAGER
# @name addClient
POST {{baseUrl}}/clients
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Contoso Ltd",
  "notes": "Key account"
}

### List projects (Slice 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Add a project (Slice 2) — ADMIN or MANAGER
# @name addProject
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Website Revamp",
  "clientId": "{{addClient.response.body.id}}"
}

### List tasks (Slice 3) — optional query filters: status, priority, assigneeId, projectId
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Add a task (Slice 3) — any authenticated role
# @name addTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Design homepage",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "dueDate": "2026-09-01",
  "projectId": "{{addProject.response.body.id}}",
  "assigneeIds": ["{{addMember.response.body.member.userId}}"]
}

### Update a task's status (Slice 3) — any role if creator/one of the assignees, ADMIN/MANAGER for any task
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS"
}

### Replace a task's assignees (Slice 14) — fully replaces the list; [] clears all assignees
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assigneeIds": ["{{addMember.response.body.member.userId}}"]
}

### Delete a task (Slice 3) — ADMIN or MANAGER only
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### List subtasks (Slice 6)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/subtasks
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Add a subtask (Slice 6) — same edit rights as the parent task
# @name addSubtask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/subtasks
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Write the spec"
}

### Mark a subtask done (Slice 6)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/subtasks/{{addSubtask.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "done": true
}

### Assign a subtask to a teammate (Slice 15) — must be one of the parent task's assignees, else 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/subtasks/{{addSubtask.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assigneeId": "{{addMember.response.body.member.userId}}"
}

### List dependencies (Slice 6) — tasks this one is blocked by
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/dependencies
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Add a dependency (Slice 6) — dependsOnId must be another task's id in this org.
### 400 if it would create a cycle or is a self-reference, 409 if it already exists.
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/dependencies
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dependsOnId": "REPLACE_WITH_ANOTHER_TASK_ID"
}

### Activity feed (Slice 7) — auto-logged: created, status/priority/assignee/due-date changes
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/activity
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### List comments (Slice 7)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Post a comment (Slice 7) — any authenticated org member, not just assignee/creator
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Looks good, proceeding."
}

### List attachments (Slice 7)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/attachments
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Upload an attachment (Slice 7) — multipart/form-data, field name "file", 15MB cap.
### REST Client extension: point @file at a real path on disk.
# POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/attachments
# Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
# Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary
#
# --boundary
# Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.txt"
# Content-Type: text/plain
#
# < ./sample.txt
# --boundary--

### Get a presigned download URL (Slice 7) — 5 minute expiry
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/attachments/REPLACE_WITH_ATTACHMENT_ID/download-url
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### List time entries (Slice 8)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/time-entries
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Log time (Slice 8) — any authenticated org member, date defaults to today, minutes capped at 1440
# @name addTimeEntry
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/time-entries
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "minutes": 90,
  "note": "Initial investigation",
  "date": "2026-08-19"
}

### Edit a time entry (Slice 8) — the entry's own logger, or ADMIN/MANAGER
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/time-entries/{{addTimeEntry.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "minutes": 100
}

### Delete a time entry (Slice 8)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/time-entries/{{addTimeEntry.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### List notifications (Slice 9)
### Trigger one first: comment on a task as a different user, or reassign a task, then re-run this.
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Mark a notification read (Slice 9)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notifications/REPLACE_WITH_NOTIFICATION_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "read": true
}

### Mark all notifications read (Slice 9)
POST {{baseUrl}}/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Reopen workflow (Slice 10)
### The target task must be DONE first: PATCH its status to DONE via the Slice 3 endpoint before this.

### List reopen requests for a task
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/reopen-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Request a reopen — 400 if the task isn't DONE, 409 if a PENDING request already exists
# @name addReopenRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/reopen-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Found a bug after marking this done"
}

### Approve a reopen request — ADMIN/MANAGER only; sets the task's status back to TODO
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/reopen-requests/{{addReopenRequest.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approve": true,
  "reviewNote": "Good catch, please fix and re-close"
}

### Reject a reopen request — ADMIN/MANAGER only
# PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/reopen-requests/{{addReopenRequest.response.body.id}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# {
#   "approve": false,
#   "reviewNote": "Looks fine as-is"
# }

### Blocker reports (Slice 16)
### Raisable by anyone with edit rights on the task (assignee/creator/ADMIN/MANAGER), at any task status.

### List blocker reports for a task
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/blocker-reports
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Report a blocker — free-text reason, not tied to a formal Dependency link
# @name addBlockerReport
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/blocker-reports
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Waiting on API credentials from the client"
}

### Resolve a blocker report — ADMIN/MANAGER only; 400 if it isn't OPEN
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{addTask.response.body.id}}/blocker-reports/{{addBlockerReport.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "resolutionNote": "Credentials shared in the client channel"
}

### Manager dashboard (Slice 11) — ADMIN/MANAGER only.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Productivity report (Slice 12) — ADMIN/MANAGER only.
### Optional query params: from, to (ISO dates, e.g. ?from=2026-08-01&to=2026-08-31)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/productivity
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Productivity report as CSV (Slice 12) — same query params, downloads a file.
### REST Client extension will offer to save the response; a plain curl needs -o.
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/productivity.csv
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
